From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Onyx contributors <onyx@localhost>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 17:29:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/20] Onyx: WTF builds (no asynchronous signals, memory
 status, newlib's feature macros)

What: libWTF.a compiles and links for PORT=Onyx.
- OptionsOnyx.cmake: -D_GNU_SOURCE (newlib hides siginfo_t, memmem, realpath, symlink, ftruncate,
  mkostemp, O_CLOEXEC... from a strict -std=c++NN compile; CMAKE_CXX_EXTENSIONS is OFF);
  HAVE_PTHREAD_SETNAME_NP no longer set (it selects Darwin's one-argument call).
- wtf/PlatformRegisters.h: no <sys/ucontext.h> for OS(ONYX). HAVE(MACHINE_CONTEXT) stays off:
  PlatformRegisters is the stack pointer only.
- wtf/posix/ThreadingPOSIX.cpp: no suspend/resume signal handler for OS(ONYX); Thread::suspend()
  is a fatal error there; the thread name through pthread_setname_np(pthread_self(), name).
- wtf/threads/Signals.cpp: for OS(ONYX), handlers can be added but none is installed.
- wtf/ProcessMemoryStatus.h, MemoryPressureHandler.{h,cpp}, unix/MemoryPressureHandlerUnix.cpp:
  OS(ONYX) beside OS(LINUX) / OS(HAIKU) (the hold-off timer, the process memory status from
  wtf/onyx/CurrentProcessMemoryStatus.h).

Why: Onyx has no asynchronous signals: a handler only runs when the process raises the signal
itself, a faulting process is ended by the kernel, and newlib's struct sigaction has no
sa_sigaction. A thread therefore cannot be stopped from another one. JavaScriptCore only
suspends a thread to scan its stack when several threads use the same VM, for the sampling
profiler, and for the signal-based VM traps of the JIT tiers: none of these exists in this port
(one thread per VM, no JIT, no sampling profiler), and reaching Thread::suspend() stops the
process with a message rather than letting the collector miss a stack.
